  "file": "src/cli/main.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "An operator edits the local configuration while a healthy daemon remains running and introduces a typo or makes the file unreadable. CLI and MCP operations then fail before contacting that daemon, even when its address and port are explicitly supplied.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/f1-adjudicate.Z3SM4M/probe.ts\"",
    "output": "Temporary probe used mocked fetch responses, no network, an explicit LIMITLESS_URL and LIMITLESS_PORT, and isolated temporary configuration files.\nvalid: CLI exit=0, requests=1; lease requests=1, result=ok; MCP requests=1, result=ok\ninvalid_toml: CLI exit=1, requests=0; lease requests=0; MCP requests=0; all report \"Invalid config.toml; fix TOML syntax in the configuration file\"\ninvalid_review: CLI exit=1, requests=0; lease requests=0; MCP requests=0; all report \"review.mode must be \\\"single\\\" or \\\"panel\\\"\"\nunreadable (mode 000): CLI exit=1, requests=0; lease requests=0; MCP requests=0; all report \"Invalid config.toml; fix TOML syntax in the configuration file\""
   },
   "evidence": "At HEAD, src/cli/main.ts:87 executes `const port = loadConfig({ readOnly: true }).port;` before resolving LIMITLESS_URL or entering the fetch try block. The default lease-client argument at src/cli/gate-slot.ts:46 and MCP backend construction at src/integrations/mcp.ts:216 likewise call loadConfig. readOnly suppresses directory creation, but does not suppress configuration parsing or validation: src/config.ts:167 throws on read/parse failures, and lines 246\u2013247 reject an unknown review.mode. At base, api() fetched using `const BASE = process.env.LIMITLESS_URL ?? ...` without loading configuration; localLeaseClient defaulted to `Number(process.env.LIMITLESS_PORT ?? 7400)`; httpBackend likewise did not load configuration. The claim's mechanism is confirmed, although 'every CLI' is broader than the evidence: commands without these client paths are unaffected, and an explicitly supplied lease-client port bypasses its default argument."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "An owner leaves a typo in config.toml, or the file is unreadable, while the daemon keeps running. From then on every limitless command, the MCP server and the default gate-slot lease client stop with a config error before they contact the daemon, even when the daemon URL is given explicitly, and stay broken until the file is fixed.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "Temp config dir whose config.toml holds invalid TOML, plus a throwaway Bun.serve on a random port. Ran `LIMITLESS_HOME=$D/home LIMITLESS_CONFIG_DIR=$D/cfg LIMITLESS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:$P bun src/cli/main.ts ls` at head, then the same command against the base tree extracted with git archive. Also ran `bun -e`-style script calling localLeaseClient() and httpBackend('http://127.0.0.1:1') with the same LIMITLESS_CONFIG_DIR.",
    "output": "head: 'Invalid config.toml; fix TOML syntax in the configuration file' exit=1, server saw 0 requests. base: exit=0, server log 'REQ http://127.0.0.1:57434/api/runs?limit=20' count 1. Script: 'lease threw: Invalid config.toml; ...' and 'mcp threw: Invalid config.toml; ...'"
   },
   "evidence": "At head, src/cli/main.ts api() starts with `const port = loadConfig({ readOnly: true }).port;`, which sits outside any try/catch, before the fetch. follow(), the mcp case, the service case and the deploy case have the same call. gate-slot.ts:46 now has `(port = loadConfig({ readOnly: true }).port, unix?: string)` as a default parameter, and withGateLease calls localLeaseClient() with no port at line 108. mcp.ts:216 has `const port = loadConfig({ readOnly: true }).port;` and runs when httpBackend is constructed. loadConfig throws on a TOML parse failure ('Invalid config.toml...') and on failed validation (evalSettings/resolveCatalog). At base, the same paths used `process.env.LIMITLESS_URL ?? ...LIMITLESS_PORT ?? 7400` and never read config. The loadConfig call inside apiTokenHeaders is in a try/catch and fails closed, so it is not the problem. Confinement does not make this worse: privateReadPaths covers only the api-token files and the DB, so confined gates can still read config.toml. Rated minor because it needs a broken or unreadable config, the error is loud and names its cause, and the same config would also stop the daemon on its next restart."
  }
 }
